# Smooth Scrolling with CSS 📜

By default, fragment jump links snap instantly to the target element. You can enable smooth scrolling with one line of CSS:

```css_not
html {
  scroll-behavior: smooth;
}

/* Offset for fixed sticky headers so content isn't hidden under navbar */
section {
  scroll-margin-top: 80px;
}
```

```html_not
<a href="#top">Back to Top</a>
```

# Link Pseudo-Classes & States 🎨

CSS provides 5 interactive states for styling hyperlinks:

```css_not
/* Unvisited link */
a:link {
  color: #2563eb;
  text-decoration: underline;
}

/* Previously visited link */
a:visited {
  color: #7c3aed;
}

/* Mouse hover state */
a:hover {
  color: #1d4ed8;
  text-decoration: none;
}

/* Clicked active state (mouse down) */
a:active {
  color: #b91c1c;
}

/* Keyboard focus state (crucial for accessibility!) */
a:focus-visible {
  outline: 2px solid #2563eb;
  outline-offset: 4px;
}
```

> 🎯 **Mnemonic Rule:** Remember **LVHA** (LoVe HAte): `:link`, `:visited`, `:hover`, `:active` must be declared in this exact order in CSS!

# Breadcrumb Navigation 🍞

Breadcrumbs display the current page's location within the site hierarchy:

```html_not
<nav aria-label="Breadcrumbs">
  <ol class="breadcrumbs">
    <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
    <li><a href="/courses">Courses</a></li>
    <li><a href="/courses/html">HTML</a></li>
    <li aria-current="page">Links & Navigation</li>
  </ol>
</nav>
```

```css_not
.breadcrumbs {
  display: flex;
  list-style: none;
  gap: 8px;
}

.breadcrumbs li:not(:last-child)::after {
  content: " /";
  color: #94a3b8;
}
```

# "Skip to Main Content" Links ⏭️

A skip link is a hidden link placed at the very top of the page that allows keyboard users to bypass repetitive navigation menus and jump straight to the content:

```html_not
<a href="#main-content" class="skip-link">Skip to main content</a>

<nav>
  <!-- 50 navigation links -->
</nav>

<main id="main-content">
  <h1>Welcome to the Page</h1>
</main>
```

```css_not
.skip-link {
  position: absolute;
  top: -100px;
  left: 10px;
  background: #000;
  color: #fff;
  padding: 8px 16px;
  z-index: 1000;
}
.skip-link:focus {
  top: 10px; /* Slides into view when focused with Tab key */
}
```
